* CMOS Inverter — Parametrized Template for Agentic Sizing Loop
* ============================================================
* Design variables injected by SpiceEditor each iteration:
*   mn1_w, mn1_l  (NMOS width/length)
*   mp1_w, mp1_l  (PMOS width/length)
*
* .meas statements compute Vm and tpd — LTspice does all waveform math.
* Python only reads the results from the .log/.meas file via PyLTSpice.

.param mn1_w=2u mn1_l=180n mp1_w=4u mp1_l=180n

* Supply
VDD vdd 0 DC 1.8

* Input pulse for transient
VIN in 0 PULSE(0 1.8 1n 50p 50p 4n 10n)

* PMOS  (drain=out  gate=in  source=vdd  bulk=vdd)
MP1 out in vdd vdd PMOS W={mp1_w} L={mp1_l}

* NMOS  (drain=out  gate=in  source=0  bulk=0)
MN1 out in 0   0   NMOS W={mn1_w} L={mn1_l}

* Load cap (realistic fan-out-of-2 estimate)
CL out 0 10f

* ---------------------------------------------------------------
* Model cards — built-in 180 nm generic models
* (replace with your PDK .lib if you have one)
* ---------------------------------------------------------------
.model NMOS NMOS (LEVEL=8 TOX=4e-9 VTH0=0.5 U0=450 VSAT=1e5 LINT=5n WINT=5n)
.model PMOS PMOS (LEVEL=8 TOX=4e-9 VTH0=-0.5 U0=150 VSAT=1e5 LINT=5n WINT=5n)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------
* Analyses
* ---------------------------------------------------------------
.DC VIN 0 1.8 0.001
.TRAN 1p 20n

* ---------------------------------------------------------------
* Measurements — everything Python needs is computed here
* ---------------------------------------------------------------
* Vm: DC operating point where Vout = Vin (switching threshold)
.meas DC vm FIND V(out) WHEN V(out)=V(in)

* tpHL: 50% Vin rising → 50% Vout falling
.meas TRAN tphl TRIG V(in)  VAL={1.8*0.5} RISE=1 TARG V(out) VAL={1.8*0.5} FALL=1

* tpLH: 50% Vin falling → 50% Vout rising
.meas TRAN tplh TRIG V(in)  VAL={1.8*0.5} FALL=1 TARG V(out) VAL={1.8*0.5} RISE=1

* Average propagation delay
.meas TRAN tpd PARAM='(abs(tphl)+abs(tplh))/2'

* Static power (just in case)
.meas DC idd AVG I(VDD)

.backanno
.end
